{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unnormalized graph laplacian clustering unnormalized graph laplacian clustering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","fileName":"Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matrix Factorization and Spectral Clustering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix Factorization and Spectral Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unnormalized graph laplacian clustering unnormalized graph laplacian clustering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","fileName":"Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering","heading":"Unnormalized Graph Laplacian Clustering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The unnormalized graph Laplacian is the degree matrix minus the similarity matrix. Its low-valued eigenvectors encode directions in which strongly connected vertices vary together and weakly connected regions can separate.\n\nSpectral clustering embeds vertices using selected eigenvectors and partitions that embedding, often with K-means. The unnormalized form can behave poorly when vertex degrees vary greatly because high- and low-degree regions contribute on different scales.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix Factorizatio